  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_SeedlingPerformance_BelowFavourableBandDose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N2df942a1eaab4986a0c725008ec1fe1e"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedFavourableBand"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for germination or early seedling growth, at a dose below the favourable band of approximately 5 to 15 Gy that Alves et al. (2027) report.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Alves et al. 2027, Radiat. Phys. Chem. 250:114279, doi:10.1016/j.radphyschem.2026.114279</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>Both band ends are approximate: the source places the most favourable responses broadly between approximately 5 and 15 Gy across its endpoints, with the apparent maximum depending on variety, endpoint and sampling time.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>Across endpoints, the most favorable responses were concentrated broadly between approximately 5 and 15 Gy. The exact position of the apparent maximum depended on variety, endpoint, and sampling time, indicating that no single universal optimum should be assumed for all tobacco genotypes.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 2.5 to 20 Gy and scored germination, hypocotyl emergence and cotyledon liberation from 3 to 9 days after sowing, and seedling fresh weight at two and four weeks, in three varieties; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for germination or early seedling growth, at a dose below the favourable band of approximately 5 to 15 Gy that Alves et al. (2027) report.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nicotiana tabacum seedling performance below favourable band dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Plukenetia_volubilis_SeedlingSurvival_AtOrAboveLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N0558084ce22c4e50b60eb49d742941bf"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/AtOrAboveReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Plukenetia volubilis for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose at or above the LD50 of 618.78 Gy that Corazon-Guivin et al. (2023) estimate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Corazon-Guivin et al. 2023, Adv. Agric. 2023:9737125, doi:10.1155/2023/9737125</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>A logistic regression of mortality on dose (a generalized linear model) gives 618.78 Gy, inside the tested range of 500 to 900 Gy.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>A logistic regression between radiation doses and mortality was calculated to estimate the optimum LD50 using a generalized linear model. [...] the LD50 of the dosimetry assay was 618.78 Gy.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 500 to 900 Gy and scored surviving plants per irradiated seed in a greenhouse sowing, with growth recorded 30 days after emergence; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Plukenetia volubilis for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose at or above the LD50 of 618.78 Gy that Corazon-Guivin et al. (2023) estimate.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Plukenetia volubilis seedling survival at or above LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_WithinFavourableBandDose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>OBSOLETE. A dose window of release 1.6.0 for Nicotiana tabacum, conditioned on the taxon alone. Replaced by a window that is also conditioned on the endpoint and the stage its source scored.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_SeedlingPerformance_WithinFavourableBandDose"/>
    <skos:definition>OBSOLETE. A dose window of release 1.6.0 for Nicotiana tabacum, conditioned on the taxon alone. Replaced by a window that is also conditioned on the endpoint and the stage its source scored.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Nicotiana tabacum within favourable band dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
