    <skos:definition>The slope parameter b of a Brain-Cousens model, which sets the steepness of the decline.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/hasRadiationType">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/SeedIrradiationTreatment"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/RadiationType"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Relates a seed-irradiation treatment to the kind of radiation that delivered it.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <skos:definition>Relates a seed-irradiation treatment to the kind of radiation that delivered it.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has radiation type</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_SeedlingPerformance_FreshMass_GerminationStage_BandUpperEndProbe">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nc3f92ef9c9e140018ed688a6883675b7"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for fresh mass at the germination stage, at the upper end of the favourable band reported for that taxon, 15 Gy. The class is unsatisfiable when that dose also lies at or above an LD50 reported for the same taxon, endpoint and stage, which flags a band that reaches its LD50 for a curator.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment>A probe for the reasoner, one for each endpoint and stage of a favourable band: it is satisfiable while the band lies below every LD50 reported for the same taxon, endpoint and stage.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for fresh mass at the germination stage, at the upper end of the favourable band reported for that taxon, 15 Gy. The class is unsatisfiable when that dose also lies at or above an LD50 reported for the same taxon, endpoint and stage, which flags a band that reaches its LD50 for a curator.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nicotiana tabacum seedling performance fresh mass germination stage band upper end probe</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/1.7.0"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.7.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <owl:priorVersion rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/1.6.0"/>
    <dct:title>OnSIR: Ontology for Seed Irradiation and Plant Radiobiology</dct:title>
    <dct:description>An OWL 2 DL ontology of seed-irradiation treatments and their dose-dependent biological effects, with dose-to-effect axioms and taxon dose windows, conditioned on endpoint and stage, for description-logic reasoning. Its classes are aligned, with IRIs checked against the EBI Ontology Lookup Service, to BFO, IAO, OBI, PO, NCBITaxon, ChEBI, GO, PATO, PECO and TO, taxa are stated with the RO relation in taxon, and its units are QUDT terms.</dct:description>
    <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>onsir</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
    <vann:preferredNamespaceUri rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://w3id.org/onsir/</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
    <dct:bibliographicCitation>Alves LFM, de Franco Rosa F, Arthur V. OnSIR: Ontology for Seed Irradiation and Plant Radiobiology, version 1.7.0. https://w3id.org/onsir/1.7.0</dct:bibliographicCitation>
    <dct:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-05</dct:issued>
    <dct:publisher rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4227-5568"/>
    <dct:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4227-5568"/>
    <dct:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9504-496X"/>
    <dct:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3521-9136"/>
    <dct:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
    <dct:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-09-21</dct:created>
    <dct:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-05</dct:modified>
    <rdfs:comment>Canonical IRI https://w3id.org/onsir; source at https://github.com/lfmalves/OnSIR</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/rbo.owl"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.56238/sevened2025.039-003"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.22456/2175-2745.146658"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://doi.org/10.69547/TSFJB.030203"/>
  </rdf:Description>
