  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Plukenetia_volubilis_SeedlingSurvival_BelowLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nac3f3b38a2fe408fa8f4aeffa918db73"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Plukenetia volubilis for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose below the LD50 of 618.78 Gy that Corazon-Guivin et al. (2023) estimate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Corazon-Guivin et al. 2023, Adv. Agric. 2023:9737125, doi:10.1155/2023/9737125</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>A logistic regression of mortality on dose (a generalized linear model) gives 618.78 Gy, inside the tested range of 500 to 900 Gy.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>A logistic regression between radiation doses and mortality was calculated to estimate the optimum LD50 using a generalized linear model. [...] the LD50 of the dosimetry assay was 618.78 Gy.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 500 to 900 Gy and scored surviving plants per irradiated seed in a greenhouse sowing, with growth recorded 30 days after emergence; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Plukenetia volubilis for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose below the LD50 of 618.78 Gy that Corazon-Guivin et al. (2023) estimate.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Plukenetia volubilis seedling survival below LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Magnolia_champaca_Germination_BelowLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N29a0abd23ff34a2781399e95206228e0"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Magnolia champaca for germination, at a dose below 30 Gy, below the LD50 that Zanzibar and Sudrajat (2016) place between 30 and 40 Gy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Zanzibar and Sudrajat 2016, Indones. J. For. Res. 3(2):95-106, doi:10.20886/ijfr.2016.3.2.95-106</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>The source estimates the LD50 by regression of germination lethality relative to the control and places it above 30 Gy and below 40 Gy. Its observations agree: germination at 20 Gy was 65 % of the control and at 40 Gy 24 %.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>Irradiation at dose higher than 30 Gy and below 40 Gy is considered being the lethal dosage (LD50) for M. champaca seeds</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 5 to 100 Gy and scored germination percentage of fresh seeds in a germination test, as lethality relative to the control; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Magnolia champaca for germination, at a dose below 30 Gy, below the LD50 that Zanzibar and Sudrajat (2016) place between 30 and 40 Gy.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Magnolia champaca germination below LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
