  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Triticum_aestivum_SeedlingSurvival_AtOrAboveLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N359c01943be34822bd1608d8d70498f6"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/AtOrAboveReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Triticum aestivum for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose of 278.61 Gy or more, at or above the LD50 of both varieties that Chakraborty et al. (2023) estimate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Chakraborty et al. 2023, Braz. Arch. Biol. Technol. 66:e23220294, doi:10.1590/1678-4324-2023220294</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>Probit estimates on survival for two varieties, 272.71 Gy (DBW 187) and 278.61 Gy (K 1006), inside the tested range of 200 to 450 Gy; the window below the LD50 ends below the lower estimate and the window at or above it starts at the higher.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>The median lethal dose was recorded to be 272.71 Gy and 278.61 Gy in DBW 187 and K 1006 respectively.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 200 to 450 Gy and scored viable seedlings 7 days after sowing, in two varieties; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Triticum aestivum for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose of 278.61 Gy or more, at or above the LD50 of both varieties that Chakraborty et al. (2023) estimate.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Triticum aestivum seedling survival at or above LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
