  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_BelowFavourableBandDose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>OBSOLETE. A dose window of release 1.6.0 for Nicotiana tabacum, conditioned on the taxon alone. Replaced by a window that is also conditioned on the endpoint and the stage its source scored.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_SeedlingPerformance_BelowFavourableBandDose"/>
    <skos:definition>OBSOLETE. A dose window of release 1.6.0 for Nicotiana tabacum, conditioned on the taxon alone. Replaced by a window that is also conditioned on the endpoint and the stage its source scored.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Nicotiana tabacum below favourable band dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/AbioticStressResistance">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/StressResistance"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">abiotic stress resistance</rdfs:label>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TO_0000168"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Stress resistance under an abiotic stress, such as salinity, drought or an extreme temperature.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <skos:definition>Stress resistance under an abiotic stress, such as salinity, drought or an extreme temperature.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_SeedlingPerformance_AboveFavourableBandDose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Ne22b068caa5e43d3b8897f39baf2cb44"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/AboveReportedFavourableBand"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for germination or early seedling growth, at a dose above the favourable band of approximately 5 to 15 Gy that Alves et al. (2027) report.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Alves et al. 2027, Radiat. Phys. Chem. 250:114279, doi:10.1016/j.radphyschem.2026.114279</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>Both band ends are approximate: the source places the most favourable responses broadly between approximately 5 and 15 Gy across its endpoints, with the apparent maximum depending on variety, endpoint and sampling time.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>Across endpoints, the most favorable responses were concentrated broadly between approximately 5 and 15 Gy. The exact position of the apparent maximum depended on variety, endpoint, and sampling time, indicating that no single universal optimum should be assumed for all tobacco genotypes.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 2.5 to 20 Gy and scored germination, hypocotyl emergence and cotyledon liberation from 3 to 9 days after sowing, and seedling fresh weight at two and four weeks, in three varieties; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for germination or early seedling growth, at a dose above the favourable band of approximately 5 to 15 Gy that Alves et al. (2027) report.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nicotiana tabacum seedling performance above favourable band dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
