    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N76f184bf935c4e25831ce9e925fedba7"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Solanum lycopersicum for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose of 120 Gy or less; at 120 Gy, the highest dose of Indrayanti et al. (2024), 59 % of seedlings relative to the control were alive.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Indrayanti et al. 2024, Pak. J. Phytopathol. 36(2):267-280, doi:10.33866/phytopathol.036.02.1047</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>The source fits a quadratic to the number of seedlings alive four weeks after germination, relative to the control, and reports 132.49 Gy, above its highest dose of 120 Gy, at which 59 % of seedlings relative to the control were alive. 120 Gy is encoded as a lower bound on the LD50, so only the window below the LD50 is defined, and it includes 120 Gy.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>The analysis of the lethal dose showed a 50% reduction in plant growth of tomato cv. 'Timothy' F1 was obtained at 132.49 Gy.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 50 to 120 Gy and scored seedlings alive four weeks after germination, relative to the unirradiated control; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Solanum lycopersicum for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose of 120 Gy or less; at 120 Gy, the highest dose of Indrayanti et al. (2024), 59 % of seedlings relative to the control were alive.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Solanum lycopersicum seedling survival below LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/bc_d">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/DoseResponseModel"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Brain–Cousens parameter d</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The upper limit d of a Brain-Cousens model, the response in the unirradiated control.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <skos:definition>The upper limit d of a Brain-Cousens model, the response in the unirradiated control.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
