  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Triticum_aestivum_SeedlingSurvival_BelowLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N004e2dbded0a45bbaa9918944659b416"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Triticum aestivum for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose below 272.71 Gy, below the LD50 of both varieties that Chakraborty et al. (2023) estimate.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Chakraborty et al. 2023, Braz. Arch. Biol. Technol. 66:e23220294, doi:10.1590/1678-4324-2023220294</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>Probit estimates on survival for two varieties, 272.71 Gy (DBW 187) and 278.61 Gy (K 1006), inside the tested range of 200 to 450 Gy; the window below the LD50 ends below the lower estimate and the window at or above it starts at the higher.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>The median lethal dose was recorded to be 272.71 Gy and 278.61 Gy in DBW 187 and K 1006 respectively.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 200 to 450 Gy and scored viable seedlings 7 days after sowing, in two varieties; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Triticum aestivum for seedling survival in the early seedling stage, at a dose below 272.71 Gy, below the LD50 of both varieties that Chakraborty et al. (2023) estimate.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Triticum aestivum seedling survival below LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Vigna_unguiculata_SeedlingSurvival_BelowLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N54dcca2b5e0847bc987a20d28539a82a"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedLD50"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Vigna unguiculata for seedling survival scored at the flowering stage, at a dose of 150 Gy or less; at 150 Gy, the lowest dose of Gnankambary et al. (2019), more than half of the plants of every genotype they tested survived.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <dct:source>Gnankambary et al. 2019, Int. J. Genet. Mol. Biol. 11(2):29-33, doi:10.5897/IJGMB2019.0174</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>The source fits a straight line to survival against dose for each of three genotypes and reports LD50s of 129.8, 132.0 and 150.2 Gy, two of them below the lowest dose tested. Its observations bracket the LD50 of every genotype between 150 and 250 Gy: survival at 150 Gy, the lowest dose, was 56 to 71 %, and at 250 Gy it was zero in all three genotypes; at 200 Gy it was zero in two genotypes, and for the third the table prints 75.86 % in both the lethality and the survival column. The window below the LD50 runs up to 150 Gy and includes it, and the window at or above it starts at 250 Gy; doses above 150 Gy and below 250 Gy fall in no window.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <onsir:sourceStatement>Plant survival was recorded at 50% flowering. [...] The (LD50%) for each genotype was estimated through the simple linear regression model considering 100% of seed germination and survival rate of the control.</onsir:sourceStatement>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 150 to 300 Gy and scored plants alive at 50 % flowering, relative to the unirradiated control, in three genotypes; where the window extends past the tested doses, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Vigna unguiculata for seedling survival scored at the flowering stage, at a dose of 150 Gy or less; at 150 Gy, the lowest dose of Gnankambary et al. (2019), more than half of the plants of every genotype they tested survived.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Vigna unguiculata seedling survival below LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Nicotiana_tabacum_SeedlingPerformance_CotyledonFreeing_EarlySeedlingStage_BandUpperEndProbe">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nd2d21c34059c4e6e85bedd438555f33a"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for cotyledon freeing at the early seedling stage, at the upper end of the favourable band reported for that taxon, 15 Gy. The class is unsatisfiable when that dose also lies at or above an LD50 reported for the same taxon, endpoint and stage, which flags a band that reaches its LD50 for a curator.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:comment>A probe for the reasoner, one for each endpoint and stage of a favourable band: it is satisfiable while the band lies below every LD50 reported for the same taxon, endpoint and stage.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition>A dose assessment of Nicotiana tabacum for cotyledon freeing at the early seedling stage, at the upper end of the favourable band reported for that taxon, 15 Gy. The class is unsatisfiable when that dose also lies at or above an LD50 reported for the same taxon, endpoint and stage, which flags a band that reaches its LD50 for a curator.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nicotiana tabacum seedling performance cotyledon freeing early seedling stage band upper end probe</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
